From 2a34050c222008c9f0130bf83924d38de290671e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phase 1 Auth Audit <phase1-audit@local>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 08:53:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Airbnb-style search, functional filters, and expand
 listings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SEARCH:
- Add a new SearchBar component (Where/When/Who/Search) replacing the
  basic destination-only input in Header. Destination navigates to the
  matching /locations/:location page; check-in/check-out and guest
  count are passed through as query params.

FILTERS:
- Extend GET /api/accommodations to support minPrice, maxPrice, type,
  guests (minimum capacity), minRating, and amenities query filters,
  applied as real Mongoose query conditions (not client-side only).
  Non-numeric values are ignored rather than erroring. Covered by two
  new backend tests plus a manual spot-check verifying the exact
  filter object built from a realistic combined query.
- LocationPage now reads guests/checkIn/checkOut from the search bar's
  query params and exposes a Filters bar (price range, property type,
  min rating, amenities) wired to the same endpoint, with a working
  Clear Filters button. Dates are shown for context only — there is no
  availability/booking-calendar backend yet, so they do not filter
  results; documented as a known limitation rather than implemented
  as if functional.

LISTINGS:
- Expand seed data from 16 to 36 accommodations across 11 locations:
  5 South African cities (Cape Town, Johannesburg, Durban, Pretoria,
  Soweto) and 6 international (New York, Paris, Tokyo, London, Dubai,
  plus the pre-existing Canmore). Verified programmatically (no live
  DB available): 36 entries, zero duplicate title+location pairs, no
  missing required fields, every listing has at least one image.
  Images reuse the existing, already-shipped Unsplash URL pool rather
  than introducing new unverified ones, since no browser is available
  in this environment to visually confirm new URLs load.

CARDS:
- Add a favorite heart toggle to LocationCard, persisted in
  localStorage (durable across refresh; not a backend-tracked
  feature — noted as a UI-only affordance).
- Tighten the listings grid breakpoints (~4-5 cols desktop, ~2-3
  tablet, 1 mobile) instead of relying on a single auto-fill value
  that collapsed to 1 column at the tablet breakpoint.

Verified: 36/36 backend tests pass (npm test); CI=true react-scripts
build compiles cleanly. Not verified: live rendering in a browser
(none available in this environment) — CSS layout and Unsplash image
loading should be spot-checked visually before considering this
final.
